    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d785">

                <pb facs="0730" n="718" xml:id="pg718"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890F.24/7–1744: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister Resident in Saudi Arabia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Moose</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jidda</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-07-17T13:00:00+03:06">July 17, 1944—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 1:42 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>214. Reference my July 7, 8 p.m. to Cairo repeated to Department.<anchor n="21"
                        xml:id="d785-f1"/> Acting Minister of Foreign Affairs informs me that Saudi
                    Government stocks of wheat and flour will be exhausted in about 3 days.</p>
                <p>Repeated by airmail to Cairo.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moose</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
